{
  "manufacturer": "LS Electric",
  "manufacturer_slug": "ls-electric",
  "model": "LSLV-S100 AC drive (built-in RS-485 Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "s100",
  "short_model": "S100",
  "aliases": [
    "LSLV-S100",
    "LSIS S100",
    "LS S100",
    "LSLV0075S100-4EOFNS"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "LS Electric S100 drives (0.4-75 kW, including IP66) using the built-in RS-485 terminals S+/S-/SG with CM.02 = Modbus-RTU, per S100 User Manual V4.3.",
  "summary": "LS Electric's general-purpose variable frequency drive with a built-in RS-485 port that speaks Modbus RTU or the LS INV 485 protocol. Monitoring sits in the S100 common area at 0h0300-0h037F, run/stop and frequency commands at 0h0380-0h03DF, and every keypad parameter has its own address per group (dr = 0h1100, CM = 0h1700, Pr = 0h1B00). This map covers the S100 common area, the trip/warning bit words, and the parameters needed to put the drive under Modbus control.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The manual prints communication addresses in hex (0h0300, 0h1103). Its only Modbus-RTU worked example writes Acc time (0x1103) and Dec time (0x1104) with starting address 0x1102, labelled 'Starting Address -1 (0x1103-1)', and the CRCs printed for that request (0x1202) and response (0xE534) are the correct CRCs for 0x1102, so the wire address is the printed address minus 1: 0h0380 frequency command is sent as 0x037F. The protocol text only says the starting address is the communication address; this map follows the worked frame. The manual states no different rule per area."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "S100 User Manual (LSLV-S100 AC Variable Speed Drive)",
    "doc_number": "S100_Manual_English_V4.3",
    "revision_date": "2026-09",
    "url": "https://sol.ls-electric.com/us/en/product/document/8652",
    "pages": "Chapter 7 RS-485 Communication Features, printed pp. 279-308 (PDF pp. 293-322): parameters and command loss pp. 281-285, memory map p. 285-286, Modbus-RTU function codes and the 0x1103 example pp. 292-295, S100 expansion common area pp. 299-306; function tables dr group p. 310-311, CM group p. 346, Pr group pp. 354-355."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Direct PDF from LS Electric's Solution Square CDN: https://sftpssqblobcdn.blob.core.windows.net/prod/largefile/document/17912520084750/S100_Manual_English_V4.3.pdf (V4.3, listed on the document page with update date 2026-10-06).",
    "Left out because the sign is not stated and the values can go negative: 0h0317 output torque, 0h0318/0h0319 and 0h0388/0h0389 PID reference/feedback, 0h0390-0h0395 torque reference/limits/bias, 0h0324-0h032B analog inputs and outputs (V1 can be bipolar), and 0h032D module temperature.",
    "Left out: 0h032E/0h032F energy (0.1 kWh and MWh registers; how they combine is not described) and the parameter-group registers other than those needed for setup.",
    "0h0305 and 0h0306 hold packed 4-bit and 8-bit fields rather than single flags; the 'bits' entries name the lowest bit of each field.",
    "Pr.13 Lost Cmd Time (0h1B0D, 0.1-120 s) is not included because its register scaling is not printed; set it on the keypad.",
    "The frequency command registers (0h0005, 0h0380) are never stored, even with parameter save; to keep a frequency through a power cycle set dr.07 = 1 (Keypad-1), write dr.01 at 0h1101 and save with 0h03E0.",
    "The iS5/iP5A/iV5/iG5A-compatible area (0h0000-0h001B: command frequency 0h0005, operation command 0h0006, status 0h000E and so on) is left out: the manual starts that area at 0h0000, which cannot exist under the minus-1 rule shown in its only example frame, so the offset for that legacy area is not settled by the manual. Use the S100 area at 0h0300+ instead.",
    "The manual prints a scale of '0' for 0h0312 output rpm, 0h0313 feedback speed and the 0h0340-0h0345 time counters; this map reads that as zero decimal places (whole rpm, days, minutes).",
    "CM.04 option 1 (D8/PN/S2, two stop bits) appears in the chapter 7 parameter description but not in the CM group function table."
  ],
